<!-- The YAM arm with a spring-loaded tong where its gripper used to be.
     DERIVED from yam.xml: the two finger subtrees and their mirroring
     equality constraint are removed, and the tong of props/tong.xml is
     mounted on link_6 in their place. Regenerate rather than hand-edit
     if either source changes.

     The tong is welded to the wrist here on purpose. This is the stage
     that asks whether a policy can manipulate with a tong-shaped end
     effector at all, so the tong is given to it rather than grasped;
     picking the tool up is a later stage and needs a free tong entity,
     which is what props/tong.xml is for.

     Hinge zero is OPEN, as in props/tong.xml, and for the same reason:
     Genesis has no springref and always rests a joint spring at zero.

     Mounted 75 mm out along link_6 rather than at the finger roots: the
     wrist's own collision capsule reaches 60 mm, and a tool sunk into
     the hand holding it is a contact the solver has to resolve on every
     step, differently on each backend.

     The two tong links overlap at their shared pivot, as the links of
     any hinge do. MuJoCo would filter that pair for being parent and
     child, but only while link_6 above them still has a joint - weld the
     arm, as a diagnostic does, and the same pair starts colliding.
     Excluded explicitly instead, so the answer depends neither on that
     nor on how faithfully a backend reimplements the rule. -->
